# Backend

## Layout

- Project: `backend/school_platform/` (settings, urls, asgi)
- Apps: `users`, `content`, `progress`, `education`, `mentoring`, `exams`, `communication`, `translations`, `subscriptions`, `fixture`, `common`
- APIs mount under `/api/` via app `urls.py` + ViewSets

## Must follow

- Public API IDs: `public_id` (`UUIDPublicIdMixin` in `common/models.py`). Never expose internal PKs in new endpoints.
- ViewSets + `DefaultRouter`; `lookup_field = "public_id"` + `UUID_LOOKUP_REGEX` from `common/drf.py`.
- Default auth: JWT + `IsAuthenticated`. Public endpoints need explicit `AllowAny`.
- JWT `USER_ID_FIELD` is `public_id` — keep claims consistent when touching auth.
- Prefer `prefetch_related` / `select_related` in `get_queryset`; split list/detail serializers when needed.
- Style: Black/isort/flake8, **line length 79**; skip formatting migrations.
- Migrations required for model changes; CI checks `makemigrations --check --dry-run`.

## Tests

- From repo root: `pytest -v` (or `pytest path/to/test_file.py -v`)
- Config: root `pyproject.toml`; `pythonpath = ["backend"]`
- Fixtures: `backend/*/tests/conftest.py`; root `backend/conftest.py` mocks translation signals
- Put new tests next to the app: `backend/<app>/tests/`

## Do not

- Invent a parallel auth or fetch layer
- Change `deploy/` / CI unless asked
- Break Kafka contract (progress ↔ code_check_emulator topics) without updating both sides
